@startuml
title SplitSmart - Record Payment and Recalculate Balance
start
:User enters amount, recipient, date and optional note;
:Call RecordPaymentUseCase;
:Validate required fields and amount > 0;
if (Basic payment data valid?) then (yes)
  :Load relevant group and balance source records;
  if (Possible duplicate?) then (yes)
    :Apply duplicate-payment policy [UNRESOLVED];
  else (no)
    if (Amount exceeds outstanding balance?) then (yes)
      :Apply overpayment policy [UNRESOLVED];
    else (no)
      :Continue with recording;
    endif
  endif
  if (Policy permits recording?) then (yes)
    :Persist Payment source record;
    :Recalculate affected pairwise balance;
    :Return payment and updated balance;
    :Display updated balance immediately;
  else (policy says no)
    :Return policy/validation error;
    :Do not report payment as recorded;
  endif
else (no)
  :Return required-field/amount error;
  :Do not record payment;
endif
stop

note right
  Confirmed: amount, recipient and date are recorded;
  amount must be positive; a recorded payment updates
  the relevant balance immediately.

  Unresolved: duplicate detection, overpayment/credit,
  misdirected payments, and which actor may record a
  payment. Policy branches do not choose an outcome.
end note
@enduml
